# Configuration — copy to .env and adjust. The Makefile loads this file, but
# only fills in what the shell environment has NOT already set, so
# `set -a; source .env; set +a` and plain `make` behave the same. CLI flags on
# the underlying scripts override both.
#
# Nothing here is needed for `make mappings`: the offline stage is a pure
# function of the committed inputs. These are for the stages that reach a
# server, and for refreshing the two inputs this repo does not own.

# --- terminology server ---------------------------------------------------- #
# FHIR terminology server base URL. Used by `deploy-terminology`,
# `upload-mappings`, `verify-curated`, and the table generators' validation
# gates ($lookup, $validate-code, $expand). Unset ⇒ the CodeSystem builds skip
# their upload step and `upload-mappings` has nowhere to publish.
ONTOSERVER_URL=https://velonto.dw.csiro.au/fhir

# PEM bundle for a server behind a corporate CA. The scripts also accept
# --ca-bundle, and --insecure to skip verification entirely (prefer the bundle).
# SSL_CERT_FILE=/path/to/ca-bundle.pem

# --- code-search ----------------------------------------------------------- #
# The model-backed mapping service the table generators propose targets with.
# Endpoints used: POST /api/v1/find-code and GET /api/v1/info.
# ONLY the `*-table` generators need it — never `make mappings`.
CODE_SEARCH_URL=http://localhost:3000

# --- inputs this repo does not own ----------------------------------------- #
# Raw ICD release files, one directory per code system per fiscal year. Several
# hundred MB, so they are not committed; layout is in README.md and identity is
# pinned in input-manifest.json (`make verify-inputs`). Defaults to ./sources.
# ICD_SOURCE_DIR=/path/to/icd-sources

# A mimic-profiles checkout that has had `sushi .` run, for `make sync-ig`. Only
# the sync reads it — a build reads the committed ig-resources/ snapshot, which
# is what keeps it offline and reproducible.
# MIMIC_IG_DIR=../mimic-profiles

# Override the snapshot location itself. Almost never needed; the point of the
# snapshot is that it travels with the repo.
# IG_RESOURCES=/path/to/ig-resources
